A||||6||Formula||Changing flexplate without dropping cradle||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||12-29-2001||11:01 AM||||has anyone ever changed a flexplate without dropping the cradle? I think it would be easier to just move the transmission 6-8 inches then to drop the whole thing? Anyone tried this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_24||12-29-2001||11:20 AM||||To make it easy, take the starter off and take the torque converter bolts off there (use a wrench to rotate the crank shaft to get to all 3 bolts).  This way you will not have to worry about getting the converter put on just right.  I did this when I put my new motor in.  I do not have any advice on changing the flexplat without dropping the cradle.  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||12-29-2001||02:17 PM||||Formula, it IS possible - remove the left tie rod and separate the left hub and knuckle at the lower ball joint, then remove the entire assembly (hub, knuckle, strut) to allow room to maneuver (this way you won't have to have an alignment done when you put it all back together). Clamp and disconnect the two trans. lines and loosen the transmission mounts. Then you will just have to remove all of the 18mm bolts holding tranny to block and it will slide back far enough to remove the flexplate. Use the advice above to remove the torque converter bolts first........<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-29-2001||04:41 PM||||The good news is you only need enough space to reach the crank bolts... you should be able to get that.<P>I'd remove the shift cable to prevent damaging the end, and gain easier movement.... take it off with the big bracket. Having it off eliminates the chance of accidently using it as a handle.<P>Don't forget to pop the right side half shaft loose before pulling on the tranny...<P>You'll likely want help for this.... transmissions are pretty awkward under the best conditions.<P>You might also want a small block and tacle or something to hold the tranny's weight. In addition to something to support the motor if needed. If either one shifts while you are working on the flex and your hand is in there,,, you could net your fingers mashed good. Just the TC weighs quite a bit. It will be next to imposible to hold things by hand long enough to get the flex.<P>If you run a strip of scrap metal/wood across the front of the tranny while you work, it may help prevent the TC moving. That thing will be a real pain to reinsert if it comes out too far. Doesn't even have to go all the way across. just bolt it to the bell to prevent the TC moving. <P>get yourself some new rubber cooler line... replace that while your messing with it. Odds are good on most cars they still ahve the original rubber. New line is cheap.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||12-30-2001||01:32 AM||||Thanks, I wasnt looking forward to this, but now it doesnt seem to bad...<P>I dropped the cradle last summer to put the 3.4 in, and it was a PITA.  the flexplate must have been faulty because it split right around the inside circle, so that it is still bolted to the motor and tranny, just in 2 pieces.<P>Thanks again!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_24||12-30-2001||10:48 AM||||Do you need a flexplate?  I have one I took out of my GT that looks great.  It is yours if you pay the shipping.  I would not suggest putting a used one in, but the offer is open for you.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula||12-30-2001||10:55 AM||||I'm going to buy a new one from ac delco, I dont want to have to change it again, the last one I bought was a autozone one and it broke.......... go figure  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Thanks for the offer though!||||reg||1
